    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6d8bb1d0-2407-5677-99bf-bad1157c0726",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $C$ and $A$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(C)=\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$C$  and $A$ only.\"",
